#### Mathematical Model

Let $I = \{\text{S1}, \text{S2}, \text{S3}, \text{S4}\}$ (production plants) and $J = \{\text{C1}, \text{C2}, \text{C3}, \text{C4}\}$ (retail outlets).

Decision variables:
- $x_{ij} \geq 0$: quantity shipped from plant $i \in I$ to outlet $j \in J$ (continuous).

Parameters:
- $d_j$: demand at outlet $j$ (from file_0_view_0, column "demand").
- $s_i$: supply capacity at plant $i$ (from file_1_view_0, column "supply_capacity").
- $c_{ij}$: transportation cost per unit from plant $i$ to outlet $j$ (from file_2_view_0, columns "C1"–"C4").

Objective:
\[
\min \sum_{i \in I} \sum_{j \in J} c_{ij} x_{ij}
\]

Subject to:
1. Demand satisfaction:
   \[
   \sum_{i \in I} x_{ij} \geq d_j \quad \forall j \in J
   \]
2. Plant capacity:
   \[
   \sum_{j \in J} x_{ij} \leq s_i \quad \forall i \in I
   \]
3. Non-negativity:
   \[
   x_{ij} \geq 0 \quad \forall i \in I,\, j \in J
   \]

#### Data Mapping

- $I = \{\text{S1}, \text{S2}, \text{S3}, \text{S4}\}$ from file_1_view_0, column "Unnamed: 0"
- $J = \{\text{C1}, \text{C2}, \text{C3}, \text{C4}\}$ from file_0_view_0, column "customer"
- $d_j$ from file_0_view_0, column "demand", indexed by "customer"
- $s_i$ from file_1_view_0, column "supply_capacity", indexed by "Unnamed: 0"
- $c_{ij}$ from file_2_view_0, row "Unnamed: 0" (plants), columns "C1"–"C4" (customers)

